WEBVTT

00:41.750 --> 00:43.168
You're back with us!

00:45.963 --> 00:51.385
Manousos, can you hear us?
How are you feeling?

00:52.761 --> 00:55.514
Do you remember what happened to you?

00:56.348 --> 00:57.766
You gave us quite a scare.

00:59.226 --> 01:03.021
The good news is that the infection
is responding to antibiotics.

01:04.772 --> 01:08.694
However, you'll probably need
to stay here awhile.

01:10.237 --> 01:12.656
You have to regain your strength.

01:19.663 --> 01:20.664
Manousos.

01:21.373 --> 01:24.501
We understand this is a lot to process.

01:24.585 --> 01:30.090
But you need more time to heal.
Your body, it needs rest, it needs--

01:30.174 --> 01:31.633
I am leaving.

01:33.051 --> 01:34.511
What do I owe?

01:35.012 --> 01:36.889
The bill! What do I owe?

01:38.223 --> 01:39.349
You owe us nothing.

01:40.642 --> 01:41.768
Not you.

01:41.852 --> 01:45.272
The real people who were here before.

01:45.606 --> 01:49.735
The hospital. Stitches, medicine.
Everything costs something!

01:50.027 --> 01:51.111
Before The Joining,

01:51.195 --> 01:55.324
your treatments from this
particular hospital would have cost...

01:55.407 --> 02:00.662
$8,277.53 in either
Balboas or American dollars.

02:00.954 --> 02:01.997
Balboas?

02:04.374 --> 02:05.918
I'm in Panama?

02:08.836 --> 02:11.173
Will you be requiring an itemized receipt?

02:22.184 --> 02:25.854
I, Manousos Oviedo,
owe this hospital $8,277.53.

02:25.938 --> 02:28.565
Plus one ambulance.

04:05.537 --> 04:06.705
Please don't get up.

04:06.788 --> 04:08.248
- Sorry.
- Our pleasure.

04:09.541 --> 04:10.542
Thanks.

04:24.681 --> 04:25.682
Thank you.

04:28.060 --> 04:29.061
Cheers.

04:29.144 --> 04:30.145
Cheers.

04:39.321 --> 04:40.447
It's not too sweet?

04:41.073 --> 04:42.991
I always worry I don't add enough water.

04:43.075 --> 04:44.743
- It's perfect.
- Yeah?

04:46.537 --> 04:48.872
'Cause I can add more if you want. Water.

04:55.212 --> 04:56.755
The O'Keeffe looks good in here.

05:00.092 --> 05:02.511
I was about to return that.

05:03.178 --> 05:04.930
We think it looks wonderful right there.

05:05.013 --> 05:06.431
I was

05:07.432 --> 05:11.478
just keeping it safe, really.

05:12.104 --> 05:14.439
There's been a lot of animals
roaming around here.

05:15.482 --> 05:16.483
Wolves.

05:17.359 --> 05:19.903
Buffalo. Buffalos.

05:21.989 --> 05:25.242
And if they were to wander
into the museums

05:25.325 --> 05:28.078
and start rubbing up
against the paintings, it's gonna be...

05:28.620 --> 05:29.830
Yeah.

05:29.913 --> 05:31.915
That could be problematic.

05:34.042 --> 05:37.713
We can secure all those buildings
if you like.

05:37.796 --> 05:38.797
Great.

05:39.298 --> 05:40.465
That would be great.

05:42.050 --> 05:43.594
Don't want a buffalo eating the Mona Lisa.

06:06.116 --> 06:07.784
I don't know what to talk about.

06:11.163 --> 06:12.456
Who says we have to?

06:15.542 --> 06:17.920
How about a board game?

06:21.798 --> 06:23.926
- Seriously?
- Could be fun.

06:28.514 --> 06:29.515
All right.

06:46.114 --> 06:47.658
So, what are we feeling?

06:51.954 --> 06:52.955
Bananagrams?

06:54.289 --> 06:56.166
No. That wouldn't be any fun.

06:56.250 --> 06:57.251
You know all the words.

06:59.795 --> 07:01.547
Chess. No.

07:01.630 --> 07:02.881
Jesus, no.

07:02.965 --> 07:05.717
Also, you're missing
a white rook, remember?

07:06.426 --> 07:08.262
But we can get you a new one.

07:11.014 --> 07:12.432
What else we got?

07:14.142 --> 07:17.813
Risk. World domination. That's hilarious.

07:18.939 --> 07:20.524
Not sure why we even have that one.

07:23.569 --> 07:25.696
What about the one you used to play
with your cousins?

07:36.164 --> 07:37.749
Too slow.

07:39.459 --> 07:42.629
Are you letting me win?
Or do you just suck at this?

07:43.505 --> 07:45.465
Keep playing and you'll find out.

07:48.260 --> 07:51.722
I have not thought
about this game in years.

07:53.557 --> 07:56.602
My nana had a blue deck and a red deck,

07:56.685 --> 08:00.814
and she used to make us put 'em all back
in the right boxes before we put 'em away.

08:01.773 --> 08:03.233
Loser has to sort.

08:06.570 --> 08:08.447
Would you like your cousin Henry
to come visit?

08:08.989 --> 08:11.658
You haven't seen him since Christmas 2005.

08:13.243 --> 08:16.747
It would be exactly
like talking to you, right?

08:19.416 --> 08:20.459
Then, nah.

08:20.959 --> 08:23.420
He didn't wanna see me these past 41 days,
why bother now?

08:26.632 --> 08:29.301
So why do they call it spit?

08:30.344 --> 08:31.887
We don't know exactly.

08:31.970 --> 08:33.639
What do you mean? You know everything.

08:33.722 --> 08:35.097
- Right? Spit.
- Uh-huh.

08:36.767 --> 08:39.227
We know it originated
in the UK during the '80s.

08:39.311 --> 08:43.273
There's different theories as to
who named it, but no clear answer.

08:44.274 --> 08:46.026
Ready? Spit.

08:47.027 --> 08:48.987
In 1986, a man named...

08:51.490 --> 08:52.491
Wow.

08:52.574 --> 08:55.285
It's like playing cards
with fucking Google.

09:00.582 --> 09:02.501
Is everyone back now?

09:03.460 --> 09:06.880
Mostly. Another hour or two should do it.

09:13.804 --> 09:14.805
Do you...

09:16.765 --> 09:19.101
You think you guys could maybe
power wash that up?

09:20.727 --> 09:21.937
Absolutely.

09:23.021 --> 09:24.064
Thanks.

09:27.109 --> 09:29.486
Well, have a good night.

09:31.488 --> 09:33.657
Carol, we can stick around if you like.

09:33.740 --> 09:34.867
As long as you want.

09:34.950 --> 09:37.160
What? No. No, no.
I'm sure you have things to do.

09:37.244 --> 09:40.622
And I've got, like,
a bunch of chores, whatnot.

09:50.841 --> 09:52.467
It just occurred to me,

09:52.551 --> 09:54.761
I never even thought
to ask you where you live.

09:55.262 --> 09:57.890
There's no such thing
as ownership anymore.

09:58.557 --> 09:59.808
No private property.

10:00.851 --> 10:03.854
Wherever we hang our hat is our home.

10:04.479 --> 10:05.480
Right, but...

10:06.064 --> 10:07.733
I mean, where do you sleep at night?

10:08.275 --> 10:09.526
We can show you.

10:27.336 --> 10:28.837
Everybody sleeps together?

10:31.590 --> 10:32.591
Why?

10:33.467 --> 10:35.219
It saves on electricity.

10:35.302 --> 10:36.386
Natural gas.

10:36.470 --> 10:41.141
It's more efficient to heat and cool
one big room than hundreds of small ones.

10:42.643 --> 10:45.896
This isn't gonna turn into the orgy scene
at the end of that Matrix movie, is it?

10:45.979 --> 10:47.397
Not unless you want it to.

10:57.282 --> 10:59.743
We make use of spaces
like this all over the world.

10:59.826 --> 11:02.538
Malls, churches, convention centers.

11:03.163 --> 11:05.832
Wait, this dog is not one of you, is it?

11:05.916 --> 11:06.959
Definitely not.

11:07.042 --> 11:08.961
Though he is a very good boy.

11:09.044 --> 11:10.963
His name is Bear Jordan.

11:11.046 --> 11:13.257
Hey. Hey, Bear.

11:14.216 --> 11:15.217
Hey.

11:17.344 --> 11:20.097
- I didn't realize you kept pets.
- We don't.

11:20.180 --> 11:24.643
But when an animal refuses to leave its
former owner's side, we take care of them.

11:25.894 --> 11:28.355
Bear is fond of Malcolm over there.

11:35.487 --> 11:37.155
Would you like to stay with us tonight?

11:40.409 --> 11:42.369
We can make you your own bed,
if you'd like.

11:42.452 --> 11:43.704
- No, no.
- In private.

11:43.787 --> 11:47.499
That's okay. I'm gonna head home.

11:48.166 --> 11:49.418
Whatever makes you happy.

11:50.294 --> 11:53.630
We can drive you.
Or you're welcome to take our car.

11:53.714 --> 11:55.215
I'll figure something out.

11:56.842 --> 11:58.302
Do you mind if we lie down?

11:59.553 --> 12:00.554
Please.

13:26.431 --> 13:28.183
We had a wonderful time with you.

13:29.226 --> 13:30.811
We're very happy to be back.

13:32.229 --> 13:33.230
Yeah.

13:39.695 --> 13:41.530
Would you like us to make you breakfast?

13:43.532 --> 13:45.158
No, no. I can manage.

13:50.289 --> 13:51.707
I had a nice time too.

15:21.713 --> 15:23.298
Hard to beat this view.

15:33.225 --> 15:34.685
Man, I love trains.

15:36.937 --> 15:39.982
There's just something about
the sound of a train horn, you know?

15:40.566 --> 15:41.567
What about it?

15:43.318 --> 15:47.197
Come on, I must've told some human being
at some point that I love train horns.

15:52.244 --> 15:54.246
I thought you knew everything about me.

15:54.329 --> 15:55.455
Not this.

16:00.669 --> 16:02.254
It is...

16:03.672 --> 16:05.257
the loneliest sound in the world.

16:20.647 --> 16:21.857
How do you do that?

16:22.441 --> 16:26.695
Something to do with
the body's electromagnetic field.

16:26.778 --> 16:29.364
Our natural electric charge, so to speak.

16:30.115 --> 16:33.118
You have one too, just unused.

16:33.702 --> 16:36.622
So... like radio?

16:36.705 --> 16:37.789
Sort of.

16:37.873 --> 16:40.250
But radio transmission is like talking.

16:40.334 --> 16:41.585
It's conscious.

16:41.668 --> 16:43.712
Our communication is unconscious.

16:43.795 --> 16:44.880
Homeostatic.

16:45.631 --> 16:46.965
Like breathing.

16:48.383 --> 16:49.426
So...

16:51.762 --> 16:53.096
No. No.

16:53.889 --> 16:56.350
There's still a lot
we don't really understand.

17:00.187 --> 17:02.022
Why do you still need trains anyway?

17:06.609 --> 17:07.986
Food distribution.

17:28.464 --> 17:29.842
Carol, you okay?

17:30.592 --> 17:32.261
Yeah. I'm great.

17:32.928 --> 17:34.638
Sorry. Carry on.

17:37.808 --> 17:39.351
Does this feel good to you too?

17:40.018 --> 17:41.478
Absolutely.

17:42.020 --> 17:43.146
So...

17:43.897 --> 17:46.275
Like... how?

17:46.775 --> 17:49.069
I mean, I know you're getting
a massage right now,

17:49.152 --> 17:52.865
but technically it's you
giving it to yourself.

17:53.448 --> 17:54.533
Yes.

17:55.659 --> 17:59.121
Meanwhile, you're simultaneously
giving me a massage.

17:59.204 --> 18:01.915
- So, I mean...
- That's true.

18:07.254 --> 18:08.505
How does that work?

18:09.756 --> 18:13.135
Does everyone feel
what you're feeling right now?

18:14.178 --> 18:16.096
Is the whole world getting a massage?

18:16.930 --> 18:18.682
No. Not exactly.

18:19.474 --> 18:21.518
It's kind of like...

18:23.812 --> 18:25.397
In the last ten minutes,

18:25.480 --> 18:31.695
there's been 1,674 deaths and 965 births.

18:32.654 --> 18:33.906
And...

18:34.489 --> 18:40.037
Just as we said this, a man in Bulgaria
was accidentally impaled on an iron fence.

18:40.120 --> 18:41.413
Oh, Jesus.

18:41.496 --> 18:42.497
It's okay.

18:43.040 --> 18:45.542
We don't think he pierced anything vital.

18:46.543 --> 18:50.380
To feel everything all at once
would be unbearable.

18:50.881 --> 18:53.759
But we know it as it happens.

18:54.426 --> 18:56.428
We're aware.

18:58.514 --> 19:02.059
Like we're aware
that you just got goose bumps.

19:08.232 --> 19:09.650
Having said all that,

19:11.568 --> 19:16.114
this massage feels... good.

19:29.461 --> 19:31.004
So, that's where it came from.

19:31.088 --> 19:32.089
That's it.

19:32.798 --> 19:34.007
Its star, anyway.

19:35.175 --> 19:37.010
- Kepler-22.
- Uh-huh.

19:37.094 --> 19:40.597
And the planet, which you can't see,
is Kepler-22b.

19:41.098 --> 19:44.768
That's our name for it.
We have no idea what they call it.

19:45.727 --> 19:48.438
It's got a radius
roughly twice that of Earth,

19:48.522 --> 19:51.650
and we think their planet
may be one enormous ocean.

19:55.279 --> 20:00.909
Sometimes we close our eyes
and try to picture it.

20:12.880 --> 20:15.007
I'm not sure I'm looking
in the right spot.

20:15.507 --> 20:17.384
I mean, I see the...

20:18.468 --> 20:20.220
the Swan, I think.

20:20.304 --> 20:22.848
Do you see a star
brighter than the others?

20:24.641 --> 20:25.642
Yes.

20:25.726 --> 20:27.102
That's Deneb.

20:27.186 --> 20:30.772
Then if you trace a straight line up
from the first section of wing,

20:30.856 --> 20:32.900
you should see a tiny dot of light.

20:32.983 --> 20:35.319
I can't tell one dot from the next.

20:35.402 --> 20:37.988
There's a lot of light pollution
coming from the city.

20:38.822 --> 20:40.657
Let's see what we can do about that.

20:49.082 --> 20:50.083
Wow.

20:53.462 --> 20:54.463
Try it now.

20:59.259 --> 21:02.012
We could place it in the center
of the eyepiece for you.

21:02.095 --> 21:03.639
Might make it easier for you to spot.

21:04.264 --> 21:06.099
Wait a minute. Wait, wait, wait, wait.

21:06.183 --> 21:07.351
Yeah, I think I see it.

21:07.851 --> 21:09.186
- I see it.
- Yeah?

21:09.269 --> 21:10.270
I do.

21:15.734 --> 21:16.735
Yeah.

21:19.029 --> 21:24.743
So, what are the people like
on Kepler-22b?

21:26.328 --> 21:28.413
We'll probably never learn
the first thing about them.

21:29.164 --> 21:30.249
They're too far away.

21:31.041 --> 21:32.918
But we know we love them.

21:33.418 --> 21:34.795
And we're grateful to them.

21:35.754 --> 21:38.423
And we'll pay it forward,
however long that may take.

21:39.049 --> 21:40.300
What does that mean?

21:41.927 --> 21:43.512
We have to share their gift.

21:43.595 --> 21:46.265
With whoever else might be out there.

21:50.352 --> 21:54.231
Just to be clear, out there, "out there"?

21:57.734 --> 21:59.653
How exactly will you do that?

22:45.657 --> 22:47.242
Can you do me a favor?

22:50.871 --> 22:51.872
Hey.

22:54.666 --> 22:55.667
Thanks. Thanks.

22:55.751 --> 22:57.002
Our pleasure.

22:57.544 --> 22:59.796
Does this mean what we think it means?

23:00.964 --> 23:02.883
- What?
- You're writing again?

23:03.967 --> 23:04.968
Writing...

23:05.886 --> 23:08.013
Wycaro. Yeah.

23:08.096 --> 23:09.640
Yeah.

23:09.723 --> 23:13.560
I had an idea and just started
filling up the whiteboard,

23:13.644 --> 23:15.604
and suddenly my marker ran dry.

23:16.188 --> 23:17.940
So, yeah. I'm writing again.

23:18.023 --> 23:20.817
Well, don't let us keep you.

23:21.818 --> 23:25.405
We are just so excited
to have something new to read.

23:25.489 --> 23:26.698
And another Wycaro.

23:27.282 --> 23:29.910
That's only if you want to
share it with us, of course.

23:29.993 --> 23:31.411
Absolutely no pressure.

23:32.871 --> 23:34.164
Sure.

23:34.790 --> 23:37.167
Happy writing, Carol.

24:43.108 --> 24:44.234
That was good.

24:45.652 --> 24:46.987
It was close.

24:47.070 --> 24:48.238
Whoopee.

24:48.322 --> 24:50.032
Don't patronize me.

24:50.115 --> 24:51.283
I'm telling you.

24:51.366 --> 24:53.952
I swear to God, when I was a kid,
I used to crush this game.

24:54.036 --> 24:55.120
We know.

25:00.834 --> 25:02.336
Are you frickin' kidding me?

25:02.419 --> 25:03.420
Jesus.

25:04.087 --> 25:05.839
You told me you never played before.

25:05.923 --> 25:07.007
Zosia's never played.

25:07.090 --> 25:11.553
But we have the combined knowledge
of every living croquet champion,

25:11.637 --> 25:14.556
so that's, you know,
a bit of an advantage.

25:14.640 --> 25:16.767
Yeah. I get that with, like,
chess or whatever,

25:16.850 --> 25:18.727
but hitting a ball is muscle memory.

25:19.895 --> 25:21.772
You guys all share that too?

25:22.773 --> 25:26.818
Maybe. Or maybe you just suck.

25:33.450 --> 25:34.451
We're doing that.

25:35.327 --> 25:37.037
Okay. Okay.

25:38.330 --> 25:43.293
Well, just for that,
I'm gonna beat all seven billion of you.

25:43.377 --> 25:45.003
Yep. So,

25:45.087 --> 25:48.549
seven billion butts about to get kicked.

25:49.758 --> 25:51.301
May we ask you a question?

25:51.385 --> 25:52.386
Sure.

25:53.554 --> 25:55.472
What was your best day writing?

25:55.973 --> 25:57.349
No such thing.

25:57.432 --> 25:58.684
Really?

25:58.767 --> 26:00.561
Come on, you have other writers in there.

26:00.644 --> 26:02.604
You should know. That's like asking,

26:02.688 --> 26:04.857
"What's the most fun you ever had
getting your teeth drilled?"

26:06.525 --> 26:08.944
You poor, tortured artist.

26:09.611 --> 26:11.613
By the way, it's still my turn.

26:15.742 --> 26:16.827
Why are you asking?

26:39.433 --> 26:42.936
This place has been closed for years.

26:51.278 --> 26:53.989
I never thought I would be back here.

26:59.786 --> 27:01.079
May we join you?

27:01.163 --> 27:02.331
Please, please.

27:05.000 --> 27:06.376
Thanks.

27:06.460 --> 27:08.378
Would you tell us what you're feeling?

27:08.462 --> 27:10.631
We'd be honored to share it with you.

27:15.385 --> 27:16.595
Well...

27:18.722 --> 27:21.141
It all started right here.
As you obviously know.

27:26.063 --> 27:29.441
I used to write longhand
on yellow legal pads.

27:30.108 --> 27:31.693
That I stole from my temp job.

27:32.486 --> 27:37.741
I had like 20 of 'em, and I'd have to go
back and forth, scratch stuff out.

27:37.824 --> 27:41.453
The whole time, I'm just dreaming
of saving up enough money for a laptop.

27:41.537 --> 27:43.789
And then I'd rip the pages out,

27:43.872 --> 27:47.251
clip them all together
with this giant metal clip,

27:47.334 --> 27:48.335
which I also stole,

27:49.086 --> 27:52.506
which took both hands to pry it open

27:53.131 --> 27:56.969
just enough
that I could add a single page.

27:59.471 --> 28:02.057
It would give me huge dents in my palms.

28:02.140 --> 28:04.059
The whole thing was a fuckin' nightmare.

28:06.854 --> 28:11.108
And there was this waitress, Bri.

28:12.109 --> 28:14.278
I loved her.
She kept my coffee topped off.

28:14.361 --> 28:17.239
She never hassled me
about hogging the booth all day long.

28:22.911 --> 28:24.246
Oh, my God.

28:27.207 --> 28:28.959
Take all the time you need, hon.

28:40.012 --> 28:41.388
This place.

28:41.889 --> 28:43.640
This place...

28:46.810 --> 28:48.395
was my escape.

28:50.564 --> 28:51.982
I was devastated when it...

28:55.485 --> 28:57.362
it... Wait, it burned down.

29:00.157 --> 29:01.283
You rebuilt it?

29:03.035 --> 29:04.745
From... Wait. From nothing?

29:05.329 --> 29:06.330
From an empty lot?

29:07.331 --> 29:08.457
We did.

29:18.133 --> 29:19.635
God, I miss those days.

29:21.595 --> 29:24.556
Working all night, so I could write
all morning, and then...

29:25.349 --> 29:27.935
I mean, those were the best days.

29:41.114 --> 29:42.574
Is everything okay?

29:52.584 --> 29:53.585
Carol?

31:08.994 --> 31:10.704
You left us kind of quickly today.

31:11.205 --> 31:12.623
Is everything all right?

31:12.706 --> 31:14.249
Yeah, peachy.

31:14.791 --> 31:16.084
Sarcasm.

31:16.710 --> 31:17.711
Yes.

31:18.629 --> 31:20.797
You want a drink? You want a drink.

31:20.881 --> 31:23.091
We'll have one if it pleases you.

31:23.175 --> 31:24.676
"We."

31:24.760 --> 31:26.345
"We think. We want."

31:27.638 --> 31:29.181
Would it kill you to say "I"?

31:30.098 --> 31:32.100
- Would it?
- Of course not.

31:33.769 --> 31:34.770
We...

31:35.687 --> 31:39.566
I... find it odd, semantically,

31:39.650 --> 31:40.943
but, of course, she could...

31:41.568 --> 31:42.569
We c...

31:43.737 --> 31:45.197
Wow.

31:45.280 --> 31:48.116
All the brains in the world,
and you can't navigate a fucking pronoun.

31:49.243 --> 31:50.577
Is this why you're upset?

31:54.456 --> 31:55.958
Where was that waitress living?

31:56.041 --> 31:57.042
Bri.

31:57.543 --> 32:00.963
On "Joining Day,"
back when she was she, not you.

32:01.046 --> 32:02.256
Where was she?

32:02.339 --> 32:03.340
Miami.

32:04.299 --> 32:05.926
Working? Vacation?

32:06.426 --> 32:09.012
Working. As a cosmetologist.

32:09.596 --> 32:11.056
Recently married.

32:11.890 --> 32:13.141
But not anymore.

32:13.225 --> 32:17.896
So, she had moved on with her life,
and then, what?

32:17.980 --> 32:23.944
You dragged her back here to do
a little playacting? Waitress theater?

32:24.820 --> 32:27.781
Carol, we're not sure we understand
what's troubling you.

32:28.907 --> 32:30.492
Can you be more specific?

32:30.576 --> 32:33.245
You are trying to distract me.

32:34.288 --> 32:35.581
Knock me off course.

32:37.457 --> 32:40.002
You rebuild my favorite diner,

32:40.627 --> 32:44.089
you jump for joy
when I tell you I'm writing again,

32:44.173 --> 32:45.382
but it's all an act.

32:45.465 --> 32:49.261
It's manipulative bullshit
because you know I haven't given up.

32:49.970 --> 32:50.971
Admit it.

32:52.055 --> 32:54.224
Tell me you know I won't give up.

32:55.642 --> 32:56.643
We know.

32:59.813 --> 33:00.939
We wish you would.

33:03.192 --> 33:06.737
But it's also true we love Wycaro.

33:06.820 --> 33:08.864
All right, honesty.

33:09.364 --> 33:11.325
Let's go for it. Cards on the table.

33:11.909 --> 33:13.118
I like you.

33:13.202 --> 33:15.329
You people. You... whatever.

33:16.205 --> 33:17.206
You're...

33:18.373 --> 33:20.876
There's a lot of things
that I like about you,

33:21.502 --> 33:23.086
but this?

33:25.047 --> 33:27.007
This is a train wreck.

33:27.966 --> 33:29.718
This is unsustainable.

33:30.636 --> 33:33.514
It's mental illness. It's psychosis.

33:33.597 --> 33:37.142
You are starving, and you can't even
pick a goddamn apple off a tree?

33:37.226 --> 33:38.477
I... How...

33:40.687 --> 33:46.985
Someone has to put the world right,
even if it means you all leave me again.

33:47.069 --> 33:49.571
Even if it means that I'm...

35:18.160 --> 35:20.495
- Morning.
- Hey.

35:23.498 --> 35:25.709
How long have you been awake?

35:26.585 --> 35:27.794
Long enough.

35:35.177 --> 35:36.887
Do you want to read chapter one?

36:18.220 --> 36:19.555
Don't leave me hanging.

36:20.848 --> 36:21.890
Raban...

36:23.767 --> 36:24.977
is a woman now.

36:25.060 --> 36:26.144
Long overdue.

36:26.812 --> 36:29.815
But I figured, now, why not?

36:30.357 --> 36:31.400
Makes sense.

36:31.483 --> 36:34.528
So, are you going to just retcon it?

36:36.405 --> 36:37.406
No need.

36:37.489 --> 36:39.241
- It can happen canonically.
- How?

36:39.324 --> 36:41.660
The Font of Truth from the second book?

36:42.160 --> 36:43.412
No.

36:43.495 --> 36:44.872
No, that wouldn't work.

36:44.955 --> 36:48.250
- No, yeah, you're right.
- The Shapeshifters of Gollinbray.

36:52.296 --> 36:53.505
I was thinking of the Caverns of--

36:53.589 --> 36:55.090
- The Caverns of Aevalor.
- Yeah.

36:55.174 --> 36:58.802
- But weren't those lost to time?
- Well, sure.

36:58.886 --> 37:02.097
But what is time to someone like Raban?

37:02.681 --> 37:04.850
They just have to get their hands
on Captain Virgil's

37:04.933 --> 37:06.852
- temporal compass and...
- Temporal compass!

37:07.686 --> 37:09.563
- Wow.
- I thought about Lucasia

37:09.646 --> 37:11.398
using the compass for

37:11.481 --> 37:13.317
something, for the life of me
I can't remember what,

37:13.400 --> 37:16.236
but it just...
it makes more sense for Raban.

37:18.780 --> 37:19.781
Yeah.

37:22.075 --> 37:24.161
So, you like it so far?

37:26.246 --> 37:27.247
Carol.

37:27.915 --> 37:28.916
We...

37:31.335 --> 37:32.419
I love it.

37:38.842 --> 37:40.302
Joe Pass on guitar.

37:40.385 --> 37:42.804
Ray Brown holding it down on bass.

37:42.888 --> 37:45.057
Mickey Roker on that blazing snare,

37:45.140 --> 37:49.144
and of course, the incomparable
Dizzy Gillespie on trumpet.

37:49.228 --> 37:50.521
And now here's a real treat.

37:50.604 --> 37:56.235
Miles Davis "All of You" on KHNM, 92.4 FM.

38:02.616 --> 38:05.577
I hope you're making
enough for both of us.

38:06.370 --> 38:07.663
You're eating too.

38:12.251 --> 38:14.294
You like omelets, right?

38:15.212 --> 38:16.213
We do.

38:16.296 --> 38:18.465
We love all breakfast food.

38:19.132 --> 38:20.801
Sure. Sure.

38:20.884 --> 38:23.720
But you... you.

38:23.804 --> 38:24.972
Like lowercase "you"...

38:25.055 --> 38:27.766
Does Zosia like omelets?

38:28.559 --> 38:30.227
Zosia likes...

38:30.894 --> 38:33.397
I like omelets.

38:34.648 --> 38:36.733
Never had many chances to try them.

38:39.570 --> 38:42.656
What is your favorite food?

38:51.164 --> 38:52.332
Mango ice cream.

38:54.084 --> 38:56.378
I love mango ice cream.

38:57.921 --> 39:02.134
There was an old man in my neighborhood
who sold it out of a little cart.

39:04.052 --> 39:08.557
I would watch the ships leaving Gdańsk.

39:08.640 --> 39:11.059
Brand new. First voyage.

39:11.143 --> 39:13.979
I was maybe... ten years old?

39:14.813 --> 39:17.983
And I was fascinated by these giant ships.

39:18.567 --> 39:19.651
Who built them?

39:20.360 --> 39:21.486
What for?

39:22.237 --> 39:23.530
Where were they going?

39:25.908 --> 39:26.992
And now I know.

39:28.619 --> 39:30.871
Sometimes, the man with the cart

39:30.954 --> 39:34.958
would hand out ice cream bars to us
when he had too many to sell.

39:35.834 --> 39:38.545
He knew we didn't have
two coins to rub together.

39:38.629 --> 39:40.839
It was just after
the country had opened up,

39:40.923 --> 39:43.550
and suddenly he had new flavors.

39:43.634 --> 39:45.636
Mint, coffee, peach.

39:46.595 --> 39:50.015
But mango,

39:51.016 --> 39:53.018
that was my favorite.

40:01.401 --> 40:02.945
Thank you for sharing that.

40:12.287 --> 40:13.413
Zosia?

40:17.000 --> 40:18.585
You're going to have a visitor.

40:36.270 --> 40:37.312
Okay.

40:37.396 --> 40:38.856
Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay.
